Notes

query - commands to interact with DB tables and manipulate data

show DBs - displays all DBs available on MySQL allowing users to view and verify existing DBs before any operations 
select database() - confirms the database currently in use
select now(); 
    .returns the current date and time 
    .useful for time-based operations
    .commonly used in logging, auditing, and timestamp related queries
    .reflects server time, not client system time 
comments - include notes/explanations inside queries improving readability and maintainability of code
auto_increment - automatically generates unique sequential values for a column, typically for primary keys in a table 
    .ensures each record gets a unique identifier without manual input
    .commonly used in ID columns to avoid duplication issues
alter table - allows modification of table structure after creation
update - updates existing records in a table based on specified conditions
    .allows modification of stored data without deleting it 
select* - fetches all columns and all records from a table without specifying individual column names






Inspecting tables:
    .describe table_name/ show columns from table_name 
    .show create table table_name;
        .returns the exact syntax used to create the table 
    .show table status like 'table_name';
        .shows table metadata 
    .show index from table_name;
        .inspecting indexes 

    